## corrections forced by these probes
B3: observed 401, not 404. The static reading said the route does not exist; runtime shows an
    auth-shielded response that cannot be distinguished from a real handler without credentials.
    The user-visible defect is unchanged (anonymous reader gets an error swallowed into an empty state)
    but the stated CAUSE must be demoted from 'confirmed 404' to 'unverified (401 observed)'.
B2: observed 401 for /api/pages, not 404. Static grep finds no such registration, so absence stands
    on static evidence only; runtime cannot confirm it while auth shields the path.
B3: /api/blog-data/slug/:slug DOES implement a correct 'Post not found' 404 — the proper handler exists
    server-side and the modern reader does not use it.

## root cause of every blocked-probe path (server stderr, verbatim, sanitized)
[Rate limit store] contact connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3306
[Rate limit store] public-browse connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3306
=> no MariaDB/MySQL listening on 3306 in this sandbox. The admission layer therefore fails closed,
   so /api/contact returns 503 before the handler is reached. No credential, DB, or browser is
   available; see M8A-RUNTIME-VERIFICATION.md for the per-claim blocked record.

